= Peer review — Simple =

Peer review is the evaluation of research work, proposals, or scholarly outputs by people with relevant expertise before or after dissemination.

Peer review can assess methodological soundness, relevance, clarity, originality, evidence, ethics, and fit for a venue or decision. Models include single-anonymous, double-anonymous, open, post-publication, and other review arrangements.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* peer review ≠ proof of correctness
* peer review ≠ replication

